  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, users can't mute or reduce the mic volume below 80% of admin accounts.\n\nThere have been times where I've seen staff on their admin account talking about inappropriate, disturbing and other controversial topics in public spaces without everyone's consent. This creates toxic environments for users, because they have to choose between being made uncomfortable or leaving entirely, both of these seem unreasonable and wrong.\n\nI think users should have the ability to mute and reduce the mic volume of any admin account, I don't see any valid reason why it should be any other way. I can understand not permitting blocks, for moderation reasons, but you don't need to force someone to hear your mic for that.",
